<title>FRANCE: TABLE- French June unemployment up 17,400.</title>
<headline>TABLE- French June unemployment up 17,400.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The seasonally adjusted number of people unemployed in France in June rose by 17,400, or 0.6 percent, to 3,130,900, Labour Ministry data showed.</p>
<p>The jobless rate, based on International Labour Organisation(ILO) criteria, which exclude jobseekers who did any work, was up at 12.6 percent.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-June month/month year/year</p>
<p> Jobless rate (ILO)	 12.6 pct    0.1 pct   0.2 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment		 3,130,900   0.6 pct   2.2 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment (ILO)	 3,222,000   0.5 pct   2.2 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		   210,000  -1.0 pct   9.7 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations  380,900   3.4 pct  -1.3 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits     335,600  -2.5 pct  -4.3 pct</p>
<p> Men under 25		   274,500   1.6 pct  -2.9 pct</p>
<p> Women under 25		 309,200  -0.7 pct  -5.5 pct</p>
<p> Men between 25 and 49    1,058,900   0.8 pct   3.7 pct</p>
<p> Women between 25 and 49  1,082,900   0.4 pct   1.9 pct</p>
<p> Men 50 and over		231,400   0.6 pct   9.0 pct</p>
<p> Women 50 and over	    174,000   0.7 pct  10.1 pct</p>
<p> Forced redundancy	     27,100   1.9 pct  -6.6 pct</p>
<p> Jobless for over 12 mos  1,123,900   0.6 pct   9.1 pct</p>
<p>In June national statistics office INSEE revised the April unemployment rate, based on ILO criteria, to 12.5 percent from 12.8 percent following its annual review of the labour market, which serves as the basis for monthly jobless rate calculations.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
